title: "TESS transit candidates and two further results, 2026"
type: dataset
# doi: to be added after the Zenodo deposit (10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX)
authors:
  - family-names: Zarco
    given-names: A.
date-released: "2026-10-19"
repository-code: "https://github.com/alejandrozarco/tess-candidates-2026"
abstract: >-
  Transit timing, light-curve tables, false-positive checks, TRICERATOPS runs and predicted transit times for four
  transit candidates found in TESS full-frame images: TIC 402710280 (P = 36.34005 d, depth about 1680 ppm,
  transit-timing variations up to 29 min), TIC 324429952 (P = 42.37574 d, depth about 1500 ppm), TIC 89247735
  (P = 18.32317 d, dilution-corrected depth 1.13-1.22 %, Rp about 8.7 Earth radii with the stellar radius from an SED
  fit) and TIC 455017950 (HD 134147; P = 40.60565 d, depth about 1310 ppm, Rp about 3.2 Earth radii). Two further
  results: the eclipsing binary TIC 11613676 (CD-30 448; P = 12.1158 d), whose eclipses were absent in TESS sector 3
  (2018), present in sector 30 (2020), 5.4 % deep in sector 97 (2025) and shallower in 2026; and TOI-540 b, whose
  transits are not detected in TESS sector 98 (2025-2026). Not peer reviewed; the candidates are not confirmed.
keywords:
  - TESS
  - transit candidates
